{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nThe Gerrit Verified route used to collapse Gerrit checkout transport faults into ordinary CI failures. A checkout 504/RPC failure happens before patchset code runs, so it is not evidence that the change is broken. Operator ruling recorded 2026-09-06/07 rejected Verified-0-on-fault and CI concurrency groups; the approved direction is in-job step-level retry for transport operations plus an explicit infrastructure-fault message if retries exhaust.\n\n## RCA\n\nThe old path had two weaknesses:\n\n1. Gerrit patchset checkout steps were single-attempt operations, so transient 5xx/TLS/RPC/dispatch faults could terminate a Verified route before code executed.\n2. `scripts/summarize_ci_failures.py` only distinguished timeout/cancelled/failed. If an exhausted checkout transport fault still made the run fail, the triage comment said `FAILED`, which implied a code/test verdict even though the failure was infrastructure.\n\nThe retry half landed in ticket `ergophobic-harassed-peacock` / Gerrit change 2823. This ticket finishes the signal-quality half by teaching the summary classifier to call checkout transport faults infrastructure faults, while preserving genuine test failures as `FAILED`.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] A captured Gerrit checkout HTTP 504/RPC failure is classified distinctly from a test failure as an infrastructure/transport fault.\n- [x] The transport-fault wording says CI could not obtain the source and that this is not a statement about the change.\n- [x] A genuine test failure still classifies as `FAILED`, so real code failures still drive the normal negative verdict path.\n- [x] The transport-fault class is visible in the run summary and distinguishable at a glance.\n- [x] Detection is portable: it keys on observable git/HTTP/TLS transport error text and the checkout job/action context, not on provider-private APIs.\n\n## Validation\n\n- RED: `pytest tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py -q` failed before the classifier change because a captured Gerrit checkout 504/RPC annotation rendered as `FAILED`.\n- GREEN: `pytest tests/scripts/test_summarize_ci_failures.py tests/unit/test_gerrit_verify_triage_comment.py -q` passed.\n- FULL: `make verify` passed with GIT_CONFIG_* variables unset.\n- Gerrit: change 2827 merged with LLM-Review+1 and Verified+1."}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1788858987838058001,"uuid":"36b1bc47-8df4-407f-bd4a-9bb1facae3fc"}